S₂ depends on S₁
S₃ depends on S₂
...
That's precisely what you want for cumulative degradation.
More accurately:
The threat samples are independently drawn, while system evolution follows a Markov state transition in which the next state depends on the current state and current threat.
That's much stronger mathematically.
